The old [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) calls this one known issue with one fix queued.
Its rendered cause table contradicts that claim. The export contains two distinct causes.
“Known” and “queued” do not mean fixed. This review describes the 4 October export, not a live desk feed.

## Separate fixes

- **Shared parser:** day-first tenant input reaches a month-first shared parser through app,
  email, or a form without the booking-v3 hint defect. For example, Harbour Dental's
  `R-41200` says 7 April became 4 July. Read the tenant's date order, not the browser's.
  Fix the shared parser and test ambiguous and unambiguous dates in supported locales.
- **Form hint:** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, but its day-first tenant form reads the input
  day first. This affects form reports from Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour.
  For example, `R-41230` reports 6 January becoming 1 June. Make the displayed hint agree
  with the form parser. A shared-parser fix alone does not correct misleading text.

Use tenant locale from the tenant directory and date order from `Intl.DateTimeFormat`.
Use the report channel and the tenant's form version. Intake tags are browser-based guesses.
Do not count by subject, intake tag, browser locale, or the number of raw export rows.

<Investigation />

## Check against the supplied views

This table runs the desk's `uniqueById`, `groupByCause`, and `tenantOf` functions.
The smaller group was merged into the larger group's ticket; it had no ticket of its own.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The weekly view separates report arrival from merge time. Do not interpret its July merge spike
as a sudden increase in reports.

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

## Change triage, not just this ticket

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is an accepted historical record.
Its subject-only rule conflicts with the rendered examples and is overdue for review under
the kb's half-year review rule. We preserve that record and replace its operational rule with
[decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause).

Different subjects can share a cause. The same subject can hide different causes.
The same form channel can lead to different causes when tenants run different form versions.
An unknown tenant is unclassified: do not merge it just because its subject matches.

<DedupeExplorer />

## Desk procedure

1. Deduplicate export overlap by report ID.
2. Read the report and resolve its tenant locale, form version and channel.
3. Group only reports with the same supported cause. Keep unknown cases for investigation.
4. File separate engineering tickets and keep report membership, counts and examples with each.
5. Check the proposed fix against both causes and the timing anomalies. Keep tickets open until verified.
6. Rebuild these views when new desk exports arrive. Review this page after a change in the evidence.

## Evidence and limits

- Inputs: `src/lib/data/reports-4471.json`, `tenants/*.json` and `desk-notes.json`.
- Running classification: `src/lib/kb/causes.ts` and `locales.ts`.
- Scope: the provided export only. The desk continues to work; this is not proof of its current state.
- The classification is a routing rule, not proof that every report body has the same root cause.
- Public engineering tickets: [parser](https://github.com/Hexrays/mega-s01e03/issues/1)
  and [form hint](https://github.com/Hexrays/mega-s01e03/issues/2).
- The source of this page is `src/routes/kb/incidents/4471-review/+page.svx`.
  Its rendered form is `build/kb/incidents/4471-review/index.html`.

